{title: Throw Me in the Sea}
{subtitle: Jonah 1:4–16}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
We sailed from Joppa bound for Tarshish
Heave away, my boys
A stranger slept down in the hold
Heave away, my boys
The Lord hurled a great wind on the sea
Heave away, my boys
The ship was ready to break apart
Heave away, my boys
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pick [F]me up [Eb]and throw me in [Gm]the sea
And the [F]sea will qui[Eb]et down for [Gm]thee
For I [F]know it [Eb]is because of [Gm]me
This great [F]storm [Eb]has come upon [Gm]thee
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
We cast the lots and they fell on him
Heave away, my boys
I fear the Lord who made the sea
Heave away, my boys
We rowed hard but we could not land
Heave away, my boys
So we threw him in and the sea was calm
Heave away, my boys
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pick [F]me up [Eb]and throw me in [Gm]the sea
And the sea [F]will quiet [Eb]down for [Gm]thee
For I [F]know it [Eb]is because of [Gm]me
This [F]great storm has [Eb]come upon [Gm]thee
{end_of_chorus}
